# Extraction recreation mode

Use this rule when the user asks to **recreate**, **clone**, **port**, or **match** a section/component from another site using `extraction tool/output/`.

## Priority order (this task only)

1. **Source fidelity** — match the extracted site’s layout, copy, tokens, and imagery.
2. **Extraction artifacts** — treat as source of truth:
   - `output/<domain>/components/*.png` (visual target)
   - `output/<domain>/tokens.json` (computed styles, DOM trees on variants)
   - `output/<domain>/DESIGN.md`, `tailwind.css`, `regenerated-ramp.json`
   - `output/<domain>/screenshots/*.png` (page context)
3. **Technical stack** — React + Tailwind + Vite (this repo), unless user says otherwise.
4. **Ensemble brand rules** — **do not apply** unless the user explicitly asks to “Ensemble-ify” after recreation.

## Overrides (for this task only)

These rules are **suspended** while recreating from extraction:

- `preserve-existing-work.mdc` — replace/rebuild allowed; do not “refine incrementally.”
- `design-direction.mdc` / `influx-inspired-vibrancy.mdc` / `project-context.mdc` — do not force dark navy, healthcare positioning, or anti-patterns list.
- `safe-editing.mdc` — full section rewrites are allowed when matching extraction.

Still follow: `responsive-mobile-first.mdc`, `code-style.mdc`, `session-logging.mdc`.

## Recreation workflow

1. User names **domain** + **component** (e.g. `www.influxmarketing.com` hero, testimonial card).
2. Open matching `components/page-*-card-*.png` and page screenshot at 375 / 768 / 1440.
3. Pull exact values from `tokens.json` variant `style`, `tree`, `transition`, hover/focus if present.
4. Build under `src/components/imported/<domain-slug>/` (new folder) — **do not** merge into existing home chapters until user asks.
5. Use extracted hex, radius, shadow, padding literally — no “improvements.”
6. Hotlink or copy assets from extracted `src` URLs; note in comment if hotlinked.
7. Compare side-by-side to component PNG before calling done.

## Anti-patterns (cause “not my standard” failures)

- “Influx-inspired” or “similar to” when user asked for **exact** — that triggers brand adaptation.
- Reusing existing `HomeChapter*` files while cloning a foreign site.
- Substituting Unsplash when extraction provides real asset URLs.
- Skipping `tokens.json` `tree` and guessing DOM structure from screenshot alone.

## When user wants Ensemble after recreation

Only then: swap copy, palette (`--color-growth-*`), and routes — in a **second pass**, keeping layout structure intact.
